<title>USA: Pa. 600 MW Homer City, Pa., coal unit seen up Wed.</title>
<headline>Pa. 600 MW Homer City, Pa., coal unit seen up Wed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 600 megawatt (MW) unit at the coal-fired Homer City, Pa., generating station was expected to resume operation Wednesday after being shut Monday, the operator GPU Generation Inc said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Homer City's unit 1 was taken off line following a precipitator wire failure, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Pennsylvania Electric Co (Penelec) and New York State Electric &amp; Gas Corp, each have a 50 percent stake in Homer City 1.</p>
<p>Both Penelec and GPU Generation are subsidiaries of GPU Inc of Parisippany, N.J.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
